{
    "$notes": {
        "font": "The rem scale from common/ux/index.css wins: 148 stylesheet usages, against 51 SCSS em usages and 0 for Const.Font. The 51 SCSS uses still read font_sizes.scss until the visual pass moves them to var(--font-*). That pass also owes `common/ux/Button/Button.styles.css`, which asks for --font-xxs — a step that never existed, so the declaration is ignored today.",
        "breakpoint": "accordion is Infinity — no CSS value can express it, so the generator emits no custom property and Const keeps Infinity.",
        "spacing": "Values are written with their unit here; Const drops the unit because its members are numbers.",
        "color": "0 is the endpoint of a ramp: white-0 #fff and black-0 #000. Keywords such as white and black map onto these without a visual shift.",
        "alpha": "Every colour also gets one variant per alpha step, named <colour>a<step>: black-2a05 is black-2 at 5%. The rgba() it carries is written here, never at a call site."
    },
